  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Period of light rain will gradually diminish and\nmove away from PA tonight and Wed. Coastal storm effects still \nlook like they will stay mainly east of PA.\n\nHigh pressure and drier air moving down from the north will \nstart to dominate the forecast for the next 7 days. Lingering \nSHRA over the southern tier tonight will pose no heavy rain \nthreat. Any RA left over in the morning could be entirely south \nof the CWA. We'll start to see high clouds from the coastal low\non Friday or even before then. We are leaving in the NBM 20 PoPs\nfor the east for the weekend for places E of the Susq R without\nany confidence to totally drop mentions of it. Some early AM\nriver valley fog is likely thru the period as our dewpoints\nnever get all that dry and the min temps will start to dip into\nthe upper 30s in the usual cold spots.",
